{
  "gate": "arc-a770-norm-fold-20261126",
  "title": "Arc A770: K1 norm_fold and K2 embed_row of the kernel plan, against kcpu.c's arithmetic",
  "measured": "2026-11-26",
  "commit": "unreleased",
  "command": "python -m kindi intel-norm --pack ~/.kindi/packs/bonsai-2b --device-name Arc --json docs/benchmarks/2026-11-26-i7-8086k-arc-a770-norm-fold/norm.json",
  "notes": "One rmsfold call (residual add + RMS + signed FWHT) per width on the A770 from the 2B pack's own sign tables and norm weight, plus the 27B's 5120/17408 widths on synthetic weights (no 27B pack on this host), timed as two enqueues with the arguments bound and one clFinish per loop. A no-op kernel gives the enqueue floor and the idle latency. The reference is kcpu.c's rmsfold/fold transcribed to numpy in the CPU's own order; the driver has no cl_khr_fp64, so the report counts how often the two-float sum still writes the CPU's float. Not a model run: attention, the GDN update, conv, the f32 scalars and the matvecs are excluded, and there is no Intel backend or support claim.",
  "evidence": [
    "docs/benchmarks/2026-11-26-i7-8086k-arc-a770-norm-fold/norm.json",
    "docs/benchmarks/2026-11-26-i7-8086k-arc-a770-norm-fold/README.md"
  ],
